{"vid":"ex1f0XkzHTM","source":"ex1f0XkzHTM.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.4,"txt":"Hello, everyone. Welcome back to the HSE"},{"t":2.4,"txt":"Coach. Today, we are going to discuss a"},{"t":4.8,"txt":"very important HSE topic, risk"},{"t":7.2,"txt":"assessment versus JSA."},{"t":9.8,"txt":"If you work as a safety officer, HSE"},{"t":12.1,"txt":"supervisor, HSE manager, safety"},{"t":14.6,"txt":"engineer, site supervisor, foreman, or"},{"t":17.5,"txt":"any other safety professionals, you have"},{"t":20,"txt":"probably heard the term risk assessment"},{"t":22.7,"txt":"and JSA, which stands for job safety"},{"t":25.3,"txt":"analysis. But, there is a very common"},{"t":27.5,"txt":"questions."},{"t":28.6,"txt":"Are risk assessment and JSA the same"},{"t":30.7,"txt":"thing?"},{"t":31.6,"txt":"If they are not same, what is the"},{"t":33.8,"txt":"difference between them? When do we"},{"t":35.8,"txt":"prepare a risk assessment? When do we"},{"t":38,"txt":"prepare a JSA? And if an interviewer ask"},{"t":41.2,"txt":"you, \"What is the difference between"},{"t":42.6,"txt":"risk assessment and JSA?\" how should you"},{"t":45.1,"txt":"answer? In today's video, we will answer"},{"t":47.6,"txt":"all of these questions in simple"},{"t":49.4,"txt":"language with practical site example."},{"t":52,"txt":"So, let's get started."},{"t":54,"txt":"First, let's understand what is risk"},{"t":56.8,"txt":"assessment."},{"t":58.2,"txt":"Risk assessment is a systematic process"},{"t":60.5,"txt":"used to identify hazards, evaluate the"},{"t":63.1,"txt":"associated risks, and determine suitable"},{"t":66.1,"txt":"control measures to reduce those risks"},{"t":68.6,"txt":"to an acceptable level. In simple words,"},{"t":71.9,"txt":"identify the hazards, assess the risks,"},{"t":74.6,"txt":"and control the risks. Risk assessment"},{"t":77,"txt":"is not necessarily limited to one"},{"t":79.6,"txt":"specific task. It can be used to assess"},{"t":82.4,"txt":"the risks associated with a workplace,"},{"t":85.4,"txt":"activity, process, operations,"},{"t":87.5,"txt":"equipment, or project. For example,"},{"t":90.6,"txt":"if we are preparing a risk assessment"},{"t":92.4,"txt":"for a construction project, we may"},{"t":94.6,"txt":"consider activities such as excavation,"},{"t":97.3,"txt":"lifting operation, work"},{"t":99.2,"txt":"work at height activity, hot work,"},{"t":101.3,"txt":"electrical work, confined space entry,"},{"t":103.6,"txt":"vehicle movement, and many other"},{"t":105.6,"txt":"activities."},{"t":106.8,"txt":"Let's take a simple example."},{"t":109.2,"txt":"Suppose worker are going to carry out an"},{"t":111.6,"txt":"excavation. In the"},{"t":113.8,"txt":"risk assessment, we identify the hazards"},{"t":115.9,"txt":"associated with excavations. These may"},{"t":118.8,"txt":"include soil collapse, underground"},{"t":121,"txt":"services, falling materials, unsafe"},{"t":123.3,"txt":"access and egress, water accumulations,"},{"t":125.7,"txt":"nearby traffic, and movement of heavy"},{"t":128.4,"txt":"equipment."},{"t":129.7,"txt":"Then we evaluate the risks associated"},{"t":131.6,"txt":"with these hazards. We consider how"},{"t":133.8,"txt":"likely an incident is to occur and how"},{"t":136.8,"txt":"serious the consequences could be."},{"t":139.5,"txt":"After that, we establish suitable"},{"t":141.7,"txt":"control measures. For example, proper"},{"t":144.2,"txt":"shoring or sloping, safe access and"},{"t":146.2,"txt":"egress, barricading, identification of"},{"t":148.7,"txt":"underground services, inspections by"},{"t":151.1,"txt":"competent persons, and maintaining a"},{"t":153.1,"txt":"safe distance from the excavation edge."},{"t":156.4,"txt":"This overall process is part of risk"},{"t":158.5,"txt":"assessment. Now, let's understand what"},{"t":161.2,"txt":"JSA is."},{"t":162.5,"txt":"JSA stands for job safety analysis."},{"t":165.3,"txt":"Some companies may also use terms such"},{"t":167.7,"txt":"as JHA, job hazard analysis, or task"},{"t":171.1,"txt":"risk assessment."},{"t":172.6,"txt":"The main purpose of a JSA is to analyze"},{"t":175.2,"txt":"a specific job step-by-step and identify"},{"t":178.4,"txt":"the hazards and control measures"},{"t":180.4,"txt":"associated with each step."},{"t":183,"txt":"In simple words, we break one specific"},{"t":186.2,"txt":"job into smaller steps."},{"t":189.1,"txt":"Then for each step, we ask, \"What can go"},{"t":192.2,"txt":"wrong? What is hazards? What is the"},{"t":194.4,"txt":"risk? And how can we control the risk?\""},{"t":197.7,"txt":"Let's use the same excavation activity"},{"t":199.7,"txt":"as an example."},{"t":201.4,"txt":"If we prepare a JSA for excavation, we"},{"t":203.8,"txt":"may divide the job into several steps."},{"t":206.9,"txt":"Step one, inspect the excavation area."},{"t":209.4,"txt":"Step two, verify underground services."},{"t":212.1,"txt":"Step three, position the excavation"},{"t":214.3,"txt":"equipment. Step four, start excavation."},{"t":217.4,"txt":"Step five, monitor soil stability. Step"},{"t":220.8,"txt":"six, allow workers to enter the"},{"t":222.8,"txt":"excavation when it is safe. And step"},{"t":226,"txt":"seven, complete the excavation work and"},{"t":228.5,"txt":"safely restore the area."},{"t":231.2,"txt":"For each step, we identify the hazards"},{"t":233.3,"txt":"and establish appropriate control"},{"t":235.3,"txt":"measures. This is why JSA is generally"},{"t":237.9,"txt":"considered a"},{"t":239.4,"txt":"task-specific analysis."},{"t":241.7,"txt":"Now, let's come to the most important"},{"t":243.6,"txt":"questions. What is the difference"},{"t":245.2,"txt":"between JSA and uh risk assessment?"},{"t":249.2,"txt":"The simple answer is that risk"},{"t":251.4,"txt":"assessment is generally broader, while"},{"t":253.8,"txt":"JSA is more specific and task-focused."},{"t":257.8,"txt":"Risk assessment can evaluate the overall"},{"t":260.1,"txt":"hazards and risks associated with an"},{"t":262.6,"txt":"activity, process, workplace, equipment,"},{"t":265.2,"txt":"or operations."},{"t":267,"txt":"JSA focus on one specific job and breaks"},{"t":270.9,"txt":"that job into individual steps."},{"t":274.3,"txt":"Risk assessment helps us understand the"},{"t":277.3,"txt":"overall risk profile. JSA helps us"},{"t":280.7,"txt":"understand the hazards and controls"},{"t":282.8,"txt":"associated with each step of the actual"},{"t":285.4,"txt":"job."},{"t":287,"txt":"Let's take another practical example."},{"t":289.3,"txt":"Suppose a crane lifting operation is"},{"t":291.2,"txt":"going to take place."},{"t":293,"txt":"In the risk assessment, we may identify"},{"t":294.8,"txt":"the overall hazards associated with"},{"t":296.8,"txt":"lifting. For example, crane overturning,"},{"t":300,"txt":"dropped loads, crane overload, lifting"},{"t":303.2,"txt":"uh accessories failure, people being"},{"t":305.4,"txt":"struck by the load, contact with power"},{"t":307.6,"txt":"lines, poor ground conditions, and"},{"t":309.8,"txt":"unauthorized access."},{"t":312,"txt":"Now, when we prepare the JSA for these"},{"t":314.6,"txt":"uh lifting operations, we break the"},{"t":316.6,"txt":"actual job into steps."},{"t":318.6,"txt":"Positioning the crane, deploying"},{"t":321.8,"txt":"uh the outriggers, inspecting the"},{"t":324.1,"txt":"lifting accessories, rigging the load,"},{"t":326.7,"txt":"positioning the signal man, performing"},{"t":329.1,"txt":"the uh initial lift, moving the load,"},{"t":331.7,"txt":"and placing the load at the final"},{"t":333.6,"txt":"locations."},{"t":334.8,"txt":"For each step, we identify the specific"},{"t":337.5,"txt":"hazards and control measures."},{"t":339.6,"txt":"That is the practical difference between"},{"t":342,"txt":"risk assessment and JSA."},{"t":344.8,"txt":"Now, one important point. Risk"},{"t":346.5,"txt":"assessment and JSA are not replacement"},{"t":349,"txt":"for each other. Both are tools for"},{"t":351.9,"txt":"controlling risk, but they approach the"},{"t":354,"txt":"task from different perspective."},{"t":357,"txt":"Risk assessment provides the broader"},{"t":358.9,"txt":"risk picture."},{"t":360.4,"txt":"JSA provides a detailed analysis of how"},{"t":363,"txt":"a specific job will be performed safely."},{"t":365.9,"txt":"Now, let's discuss the basic steps of"},{"t":369.9,"txt":"risk assessment. Step one, identify the"},{"t":372.6,"txt":"hazards. Step two, identify who may be"},{"t":375.6,"txt":"harmed and how. Step three, evaluate the"},{"t":378.5,"txt":"risk. Step four, determine appropriate"},{"t":382.1,"txt":"control measures. Step five, implement"},{"t":385.6,"txt":"the controls. And step six, review and"},{"t":388.4,"txt":"update the assessment when necessary."},{"t":391.6,"txt":"Risk assessment is not always a one-time"},{"t":394.4,"txt":"activity. If site condition change,"},{"t":396.9,"txt":"equipment changes, the work method"},{"t":399,"txt":"changes, or an incident or near miss"},{"t":401.6,"txt":"occur, the risk assessment may need to"},{"t":404.4,"txt":"be reviewed and updated."},{"t":407.2,"txt":"Now, let's understand the basic steps of"},{"t":409,"txt":"a JSA."},{"t":410.5,"txt":"First, select the specific job. Then,"},{"t":413.9,"txt":"break the job into logical steps."},{"t":416.4,"txt":"Identify the hazards associated with"},{"t":419.1,"txt":"each step. Evaluate the risk. Establish"},{"t":421.7,"txt":"control measures. Explain the JSA to the"},{"t":425,"txt":"workers involved. And finally, monitor"},{"t":428,"txt":"the work to make sure that the actual"},{"t":430.8,"txt":"job is being performed according to the"},{"t":433.5,"txt":"agreed controls."},{"t":435.6,"txt":"If site conditions change, the JSA"},{"t":438.2,"txt":"should also be reviewed and revised when"},{"t":440.9,"txt":"required."},{"t":442.4,"txt":"Now,"},{"t":443.4,"txt":"let's look at this from an interview"},{"t":445.8,"txt":"point of view. Suppose the interviewer"},{"t":448,"txt":"asks you,"},{"t":449.1,"txt":"\"What is the difference between risk"},{"t":450.4,"txt":"assessment and JSA?\" You can give an"},{"t":452.8,"txt":"answer like this."},{"t":454.9,"txt":"Risk assessment is a systematic process"},{"t":457.2,"txt":"used to identify hazards, evaluate"},{"t":459.8,"txt":"risks, and establish control measures"},{"t":462.2,"txt":"for a workplace activity, process, or"},{"t":465.1,"txt":"operation. JSA or job safety analysis is"},{"t":469.1,"txt":"a task-specific method in which a"},{"t":471,"txt":"particular job is broken down into"},{"t":473.4,"txt":"individual steps, and the hazards and"},{"t":475.5,"txt":"control measures for each step are"},{"t":478.2,"txt":"identified."},{"t":479.6,"txt":"If the interviewer asks you for a"},{"t":481.5,"txt":"practical example, you can say, \"For"},{"t":483.9,"txt":"example, a lifting operations may have"},{"t":486.6,"txt":"an overall risk assessment covering"},{"t":488.8,"txt":"hazards such as crane overturning,"},{"t":491.2,"txt":"dropped loads, overload lifting"},{"t":494.3,"txt":"accessories failure, and contact with"},{"t":496.6,"txt":"power lines."},{"t":497.8,"txt":"The JSA will break the actual lifting"},{"t":500.3,"txt":"activity into steps such as crane setup,"},{"t":503.8,"txt":"rigging, initial lifting, load movement,"},{"t":507,"txt":"and load placement with specific hazards"},{"t":509.6,"txt":"and controls"},{"t":511.2,"txt":"identified for each step.\" This is a"},{"t":513.9,"txt":"simple and professional way to explain"},{"t":515.9,"txt":"the difference during a interview."},{"t":518.8,"txt":"If you found this video helpful,"},{"t":521,"txt":"make sure to like, share, and subscribe"},{"t":522.6,"txt":"to the HSE Coach."},{"t":524.7,"txt":"And if you have not subscribed to the"},{"t":527.2,"txt":"HSE Coach yet, please uh subscribe and"},{"t":529.8,"txt":"press the bell icon. I will see you in"},{"t":532.2,"txt":"the next video with another practical"},{"t":534.3,"txt":"HSE topic. Till then, take care."},{"t":536.6,"txt":"Bye-bye."}],"words":[{"t":0.36,"w":"Hello,"},{"t":0.6,"w":"everyone."},{"t":1.04,"w":"Welcome"},{"t":1.4,"w":"back"},{"t":1.72,"w":"to"},{"t":1.84,"w":"the"},{"t":2.04,"w":"HSE"},{"t":2.4,"w":"Coach."},{"t":3.24,"w":"Today,"},{"t":3.48,"w":"we"},{"t":3.72,"w":"are"},{"t":3.84,"w":"going"},{"t":4.08,"w":"to"},{"t":4.16,"w":"discuss"},{"t":4.64,"w":"a"},{"t":4.76,"w":"very"},{"t":5.2,"w":"important"},{"t":5.8,"w":"HSE"},{"t":6.2,"w":"topic,"},{"t":6.92,"w":"risk"},{"t":7.2,"w":"assessment"},{"t":7.88,"w":"versus"},{"t":8.68,"w":"JSA."},{"t":9.8,"w":"If"},{"t":9.92,"w":"you"},{"t":10.04,"w":"work"},{"t":10.36,"w":"as"},{"t":10.56,"w":"a"},{"t":10.64,"w":"safety"},{"t":11,"w":"officer,"},{"t":11.72,"w":"HSE"},{"t":12.12,"w":"supervisor,"},{"t":13.12,"w":"HSE"},{"t":13.56,"w":"manager,"},{"t":14.24,"w":"safety"},{"t":14.64,"w":"engineer,"},{"t":15.44,"w":"site"},{"t":15.72,"w":"supervisor,"},{"t":16.44,"w":"foreman,"},{"t":17.16,"w":"or"},{"t":17.48,"w":"any"},{"t":17.92,"w":"other"},{"t":18.12,"w":"safety"},{"t":18.44,"w":"professionals,"},{"t":19.28,"w":"you"},{"t":19.48,"w":"have"},{"t":19.96,"w":"probably"},{"t":20.6,"w":"heard"},{"t":21.08,"w":"the"},{"t":21.28,"w":"term"},{"t":21.92,"w":"risk"},{"t":22.16,"w":"assessment"},{"t":22.72,"w":"and"},{"t":22.92,"w":"JSA,"},{"t":23.76,"w":"which"},{"t":23.96,"w":"stands"},{"t":24.32,"w":"for"},{"t":24.76,"w":"job"},{"t":25,"w":"safety"},{"t":25.28,"w":"analysis."},{"t":26.36,"w":"But,"},{"t":26.48,"w":"there"},{"t":26.68,"w":"is"},{"t":26.84,"w":"a"},{"t":26.92,"w":"very"},{"t":27.2,"w":"common"},{"t":27.52,"w":"questions."},{"t":28.64,"w":"Are"},{"t":28.8,"w":"risk"},{"t":29.04,"w":"assessment"},{"t":29.56,"w":"and"},{"t":29.76,"w":"JSA"},{"t":30.16,"w":"the"},{"t":30.36,"w":"same"},{"t":30.68,"w":"thing?"},{"t":31.64,"w":"If"},{"t":31.72,"w":"they"},{"t":31.88,"w":"are"},{"t":32.04,"w":"not"},{"t":32.52,"w":"same,"},{"t":33.36,"w":"what"},{"t":33.52,"w":"is"},{"t":33.64,"w":"the"},{"t":33.76,"w":"difference"},{"t":34.12,"w":"between"},{"t":34.44,"w":"them?"},{"t":35.28,"w":"When"},{"t":35.48,"w":"do"},{"t":35.64,"w":"we"},{"t":35.8,"w":"prepare"},{"t":36.32,"w":"a"},{"t":36.4,"w":"risk"},{"t":36.64,"w":"assessment?"},{"t":37.24,"w":"When"},{"t":37.48,"w":"do"},{"t":37.64,"w":"we"},{"t":38.04,"w":"prepare"},{"t":38.52,"w":"a"},{"t":38.64,"w":"JSA?"},{"t":39.64,"w":"And"},{"t":39.92,"w":"if"},{"t":40.16,"w":"an"},{"t":40.28,"w":"interviewer"},{"t":40.92,"w":"ask"},{"t":41.24,"w":"you,"},{"t":41.4,"w":"\"What"},{"t":41.6,"w":"is"},{"t":41.76,"w":"the"},{"t":41.84,"w":"difference"},{"t":42.2,"w":"between"},{"t":42.6,"w":"risk"},{"t":42.84,"w":"assessment"},{"t":43.28,"w":"and"},{"t":43.44,"w":"JSA?\""},{"t":44.16,"w":"how"},{"t":44.36,"w":"should"},{"t":44.68,"w":"you"},{"t":45.08,"w":"answer?"},{"t":45.88,"w":"In"},{"t":46.04,"w":"today's"},{"t":46.4,"w":"video,"},{"t":46.68,"w":"we"},{"t":46.84,"w":"will"},{"t":47.08,"w":"answer"},{"t":47.56,"w":"all"},{"t":47.92,"w":"of"},{"t":48.04,"w":"these"},{"t":48.24,"w":"questions"},{"t":48.76,"w":"in"},{"t":48.96,"w":"simple"},{"t":49.4,"w":"language"},{"t":50.12,"w":"with"},{"t":50.36,"w":"practical"},{"t":50.88,"w":"site"},{"t":51.12,"w":"example."},{"t":51.96,"w":"So,"},{"t":52.12,"w":"let's"},{"t":52.36,"w":"get"},{"t":52.52,"w":"started."},{"t":54.04,"w":"First,"},{"t":54.64,"w":"let's"},{"t":54.88,"w":"understand"},{"t":55.76,"w":"what"},{"t":56.04,"w":"is"},{"t":56.48,"w":"risk"},{"t":56.76,"w":"assessment."},{"t":58.2,"w":"Risk"},{"t":58.44,"w":"assessment"},{"t":58.96,"w":"is"},{"t":59.16,"w":"a"},{"t":59.4,"w":"systematic"},{"t":60.04,"w":"process"},{"t":60.52,"w":"used"},{"t":60.8,"w":"to"},{"t":60.92,"w":"identify"},{"t":61.52,"w":"hazards,"},{"t":62.32,"w":"evaluate"},{"t":62.88,"w":"the"},{"t":63.12,"w":"associated"},{"t":63.92,"w":"risks,"},{"t":64.4,"w":"and"},{"t":64.6,"w":"determine"},{"t":65.56,"w":"suitable"},{"t":66.08,"w":"control"},{"t":66.44,"w":"measures"},{"t":66.88,"w":"to"},{"t":67.08,"w":"reduce"},{"t":67.84,"w":"those"},{"t":68.24,"w":"risks"},{"t":